f9"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commit/e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6","sha":"e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commits/e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6"}],"sha":"ceb8ba92e3eafa03b3547c4f43c38877912671f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commits/ceb8ba92e3eafa03b3547c4f43c38877912671f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45439239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahmoudelshaieb","id":45439239,"login":"mahmoudelshaieb","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDM5MjM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commits/e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:54:05Z","email":"elshaieb_career@outlook.com","name":"mahmoudelshaieb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:54:05Z","email":"elshaieb_career@outlook.com","name":"mahmoudelshaieb"},"message":"Add the flynas design impact case study\n\nSix months of design work at flynas — operations, customer experience,\ncabin crew, design foundations — sourced from the internal review deck\n(design-impact.pdf). It leads the work index as the most recent work.\n\nEvery project slide in the deck uses one spine: category, title, then\nlabeled PROBLEM / APPROACH / RESULT blocks beside a device mockup. No\nexisting component renders a three-part labeled block, so this adds\ncomponents/ImpactCard and a matching \"impact\" section kind in\nBentoCaseStudy. Labels live per block, so slide 05''s CONTRIBUTION variant\nneeds no special case, and a block with no label renders as plain body\ncopy (used for the Sky Buddy card, which the deck leaves uncaptioned).\n\nImpactMetrics previously hardcoded col-4, a fixed 3-up row; this study\nhas 4 metrics. It now derives the column width from the item count, so\n3 metrics still render col-4 and 4 render col-3. Verified inert: built\nthe parent commit in a separate worktree and diffed rendered DOM for\nboth bento studies plus /driving-app and /about — all identical once\nreact-medium-image-zoom''s per-render random ids are normalized.\n\nAssets are cropped from the deck (poppler is not installed; a Swift +\nPDFKit helper renders pages, PIL crops and encodes WebP). Mockup bounds\nare detected per slide rather than hand-measured. 396 KB for six images.\nSlides 02, 08 and 09 render without their visuals, so the design system\nand component library sections are text-only until real exports land.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"076434feb0b1d6561283b5af36c358e2b6d40bf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/git/trees/076434feb0b1d6561283b5af36c358e2b6d40bf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/git/commits/e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45439239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahmoudelshaieb","id":45439239,"login":"mahmoudelshaieb","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDM5MjM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commit/e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6","node_id":"C_kwDOFquSLtoAKGUxYmExYWU0Yjk0ZDNiODc0OWE2ZGFkMzg0Y2Q0MDE3ZDVjYTcwYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commit/f4b913a3fa17af9125f5ab62627740f593fb825e","sha":"f4b913a3fa17af9125f5ab62627740f593fb825e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commits/f4b913a3fa17af9125f5ab62627740f593fb825e"}],"sha":"e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commits/e1ba1ae4b94d3b8749a6dad384cd4017d5ca70a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45439239?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahmoudelshaieb","id":45439239,"login":"mahmoudelshaieb","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDM5MjM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahmoudelshaieb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/commits/f4b913a3fa17af9125f5ab62627740f593fb825e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:22:40Z","email":"elshaieb_career@outlook.com","name":"mahmoudelshaieb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T11:22:40Z","email":"elshaieb_career@outlook.com","name":"mahmoudelshaieb"},"message":"Document the real fix for the root-owned node_modules EACCES\n\nnode_modules/ was owned by root, so every cache write failed: the dev\nserver showed a full-screen \"Compiled with problems:\" overlay and died on\nthe next rebuild, and yarn build failed outright.\n\nThe tree is now user-owned, so plain `yarn start` and `yarn build` work\nand the CI=false/DISABLE_ESLINT_PLUGIN workaround these docs used to\nrecommend is obsolete. Replaced it with the symptom and the two real\nfixes, and a warning that DISABLE_ESLINT_PLUGIN only dodges the ESLint\ncache before webpack''s own cache write fails.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"edab35a1748ed220ff16da7683e96654374c51ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/git/trees/edab35a1748ed220ff16da7683e96654374c51ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mahmoudelshaieb/Personal-plan/git/commits/f4b913a3fa17af9125f5ab62627740f593fb825e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_a